  "measurement_notes": [
    "Latencies are wall-clock around Adapter::predict only; normalization and validation are outside the timed region.",
    "External-process adapters include JSON-lines serialization and pipe transfer in every latency; native adapters do not. Compare transports with that in mind.",
    "Cold = a fresh process start with model files likely in the OS page cache after the first run; true cold-disk start is not forced. For native adapters each cold sample is a fresh evaluator child process (no spawn or pipe cost in the sample: only open and the first batch are timed).",
    "Warm = the same process after `warmup_batches` untimed batches. Each cell is repeated `repeats` times; the cell's top-level numbers are the lower-median repeat and `summary` carries median and spread over repeats.",
    "Native memory: `in-process-isolated` is the peak RSS of a dedicated child holding only the workload; `baseline_rss_bytes` is its peak before the adapter opened.",
    "Cells and repeats run serially on an otherwise unmanaged machine; the protocol does not control CPU frequency, thermal state or background load."
  ],
